# W9, Ctrl-C (ADR-0110 item 4): W8 at -j4 in the foreground, interrupted
# from the terminal while tables are being written: TASK-02b's 1.5 s was the
# middle of a 4 s build, and here, on one CPU and at this kernel's speed,
# 1.5 s is still before the first table (review R1), so the interrupt waits
# for make's output to show the leaves' tables under way. make's output goes
# to the terminal, as tools/posix-surface/remote/w9_session.py had it. dash
# abandons the rest of a line after its foreground job died of SIGINT, so
# the status, the partial targets and the processes left are asked on lines
# of their own, as w9_session.py asked them.
! -FAIL
! panicked
! ZORAYA-FAULT
< PSURF> 
> cd /work/w9-int && make -j4\r
% boot
< ./mktab 2 > t2.h
~ 300 PSURF>
> \x03
< Deleting file 't
< PSURF> 
% w9-int
> echo W9-STATUS $?\r
< W9-STATUS 130
< PSURF> 
> sh /tests/w9-check.sh /work/w9-int\r
< W9-PARTIAL 0
< PSURF> 
> sleep 0.5; t_posix live 3000\r
< W9-LEFT 0
< PSURF> 
> exit\r
< POSIX-STATS images=
< POSIX-CALLS
< BROKER-STATS
